{"uid": "own/0007", "dataset": "own", "topic": "systems", "model_alias": "opus", "model_id": "claude-opus-5-5", "answer_ref": "7", "answer_extracted": "7", "correct": true, "grade_method": "exact", "input_tokens": 101, "output_tokens": 109, "cost_usd": 0.002584, "latency_s": 1.7730679512023926, "stop_reason": "end_turn", "from_cache": false, "output_text": "Add the two equations so that y cancels:\n\n(x + y) + (x − y) = 10 + 4\n\n2x = 14\n\nx = 7\n\nTo check, substitute x = 7 into the first equation to get y = 3. Then 7 + 3 = 10 and 7 − 3 = 4, so both equations hold.\n\n\\boxed{7}"}
{"uid": "own/0009", "dataset": "own", "topic": "arithmetic", "model_alias": "haiku", "model_id": "claude-haiku-5-5", "answer_ref": "16", "answer_extracted": "16", "correct": true, "grade_method": "exact", "input_tokens": 101, "output_tokens": 65, "cost_usd": 4.26e-05, "latency_s": 0.9291815757751465, "stop_reason": "end_turn", "from_cache": false, "output_text": "240 divided by 15 is 16 exactly, since 15 × 16 = 240. Every row is full, so there are no leftover plants.\n\nNumber of complete rows: 16\n\n\\boxed{16}"}
