{"uid": "own/0009", "dataset": "own", "topic": "arithmetic", "model_alias": "sonnet", "model_id": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "answer_ref": "16", "answer_extracted": "16", "correct": true, "grade_method": "exact", "input_tokens": 101, "output_tokens": 144, "cost_usd": 0.001642, "latency_s": 1.8445022106170654, "stop_reason": "end_turn", "from_cache": false, "output_text": "Each complete row uses 15 plants, so the number of complete rows is 240 ÷ 15 = 16.\n\nCheck: 16 × 15 = 240, so there are no plants left over.\n\n\\boxed{16}"}
{"uid": "own/0010", "dataset": "own", "topic": "percentages", "model_alias": "haiku", "model_id": "claude-haiku-5-5", "answer_ref": "50", "answer_extracted": "50", "correct": true, "grade_method": "exact", "input_tokens": 99, "output_tokens": 76, "cost_usd": 4.79e-05, "latency_s": 1.2110142707824707, "stop_reason": "end_turn", "from_cache": false, "output_text": "If the discounted price is 80% of the original price, then:\n\n0.8 × P = 40\n\nP = 40 / 0.8 = 50\n\nCheck: a 20% discount on $50 is $10, leaving $40.\n\n\\boxed{50}"}
{"uid": "own/0010", "dataset": "own", "topic": "percentages", "model_alias": "sonnet", "model_id": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "answer_ref": "50", "answer_extracted": "50", "correct": true, "grade_method": "exact", "input_tokens": 99, "output_tokens": 93, "cost_usd": 0.0011279999999999999, "latency_s": 1.7036845684051514, "stop_reason": "end_turn", "from_cache": false, "output_text": "After a 20% discount, the customer pays 80% of the original price. Let the original price be P.\n\n0.8P = 40\n\nP = 40 / 0.8 = 50\n\nCheck: 20% of 50 is 10, and 50 − 10 = 40, which matches.\n\n\\boxed{50}"}
{"uid": "own/0009", "dataset": "own", "topic": "arithmetic", "model_alias": "opus", "model_id": "claude-opus-5-5", "answer_ref": "16", "answer_extracted": "16", "correct": true, "grade_method": "exact", "input_tokens": 101, "output_tokens": 104, "cost_usd": 0.0024839999999999997, "latency_s": 1.9439823627471924, "stop_reason": "end_turn", "from_cache": false, "output_text": "To find the number of complete rows, divide the total number of plants by the number of plants per row:\n\n$$240 \\div 15 = 16.$$\n\nCheck: $15 \\times 16 = 240$, so the division is exact. All 16 rows are complete and no plants are left over.\n\n\\boxed{16}"}
{"uid": "own/0011", "dataset": "own", "topic": "algebra", "model_alias": "haiku", "model_id": "claude-haiku-5-5", "answer_ref": "7", "answer_extracted": "7", "correct": true, "grade_method": "exact", "input_tokens": 91, "output_tokens": 51, "cost_usd": 3.46e-05, "latency_s": 0.891913652420044, "stop_reason": "end_turn", "from_cache": false, "output_text": "Since x² = 49, we have x = ±7. The problem specifies that x is positive, so we take the positive root.\n\nx = 7\n\n\\boxed{7}"}
{"uid": "own/0010", "dataset": "own", "topic": "percentages", "model_alias": "opus", "model_id": "claude-opus-5-5", "answer_ref": "50", "answer_extracted": "50", "correct": true, "grade_method": "exact", "input_tokens": 99, "output_tokens": 121, "cost_usd": 0.002816, "latency_s": 1.9167451858520508, "stop_reason": "end_turn", "from_cache": false, "output_text": "A 20% discount means the sale price is 80% of the original price.\n\nLet $x$ be the original price. Then\n\n$$0.8x = 40$$\n\n$$x = \\frac{40}{0.8} = 50$$\n\nCheck: 20% of 50 is 10, and $50 - 10 = 40$. ✓\n\n\\boxed{50}"}
{"uid": "own/0012", "dataset": "own", "topic": "interest", "model_alias": "haiku", "model_id": "claude-haiku-5-5", "answer_ref": "100", "answer_extracted": "100", "correct": true, "grade_method": "exact", "input_tokens": 113, "output_tokens": 125, "cost_usd": 7.38e-05, "latency_s": 1.0436172485351562, "stop_reason": "end_turn", "from_cache": false, "output_text": "Simple interest is computed as I = P × r × t.\n\nHere P = 1000 dollars, r = 0.05 per year, and t = 2 years.\n\nI = 1000 × 0.05 × 2 = 100 dollars.\n\nCheck: each year earns 1000 × 0.05 = 50 dollars, and over 2 years that totals 100 dollars.\n\n\\boxed{100}"}
{"uid": "own/0011", "dataset": "own", "topic": "algebra", "model_alias": "sonnet", "model_id": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "answer_ref": "7", "answer_extracted": "7", "correct": true, "grade_method": "exact", "input_tokens": 91, "output_tokens": 44, "cost_usd": 0.0006219999999999999, "latency_s": 1.5881929397583008, "stop_reason": "end_turn", "from_cache": false, "output_text": "Since x² = 49, x = 7 or x = −7. Because x is positive, we discard x = −7.\n\n\\boxed{7}"}
{"uid": "own/0011", "dataset": "own", "topic": "algebra", "model_alias": "opus", "model_id": "claude-opus-5-5", "answer_ref": "7", "answer_extracted": "7", "correct": true, "grade_method": "exact", "input_tokens": 91, "output_tokens": 79, "cost_usd": 0.0019439999999999998, "latency_s": 1.9544916152954102, "stop_reason": "end_turn", "from_cache": false, "output_text": "Solve $x^2 = 49$:\n\n$$x = \\pm\\sqrt{49} = \\pm 7.$$\n\nSince $x$ must be positive, we discard $-7$, which leaves $x = 7$.\n\n\\boxed{7}"}
{"uid": "own/0012", "dataset": "own", "topic": "interest", "model_alias": "sonnet", "model_id": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "answer_ref": "100", "answer_extracted": "100", "correct": true, "grade_method": "exact", "input_tokens": 113, "output_tokens": 110, "cost_usd": 0.0013260000000000001, "latency_s": 1.1731081008911133, "stop_reason": "end_turn", "from_cache": false, "output_text": "Simple interest is calculated as I = P · r · t, where P is the principal, r is the annual rate, and t is the time in years.\n\nHere P = 1000, r = 0.05, and t = 2, so\n\nI = 1000 × 0.05 × 2 = 100.\n\nThe total interest earned is 100 dollars.\n\n\\boxed{100}"}
{"uid": "own/0013", "dataset": "own", "topic": "statistics", "model_alias": "haiku", "model_id": "claude-haiku-5-5", "answer_ref": "8", "answer_extracted": "8", "correct": true, "grade_method": "exact", "input_tokens": 92, "output_tokens": 65, "cost_usd": 4.17e-05, "latency_s": 0.88175368309021, "stop_reason": "end_turn", "from_cache": false, "output_text": "The average of the three grades is the sum divided by the number of grades:\n\n$$\\frac{7 + 8 + 9}{3} = \\frac{24}{3} = 8$$\n\n\\boxed{8}"}
{"uid": "own/0012", "dataset": "own", "topic": "interest", "model_alias": "opus", "model_id": "claude-opus-5-5", "answer_ref": "100", "answer_extracted": "100", "correct": true, "grade_method": "exact", "input_tokens": 113, "output_tokens": 103, "cost_usd": 0.002512, "latency_s": 1.8498401641845703, "stop_reason": "end_turn", "from_cache": false, "output_text": "Simple interest is found with I = P × r × t.\n\n- Principal P = 1000 dollars\n- Rate r = 5% = 0.05 per year\n- Time t = 2 years\n\nI = 1000 × 0.05 × 2 = 100\n\nThe total interest earned is 100 dollars.\n\n\\boxed{100}"}
{"uid": "own/0013", "dataset": "own", "topic": "statistics", "model_alias": "sonnet", "model_id": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "answer_ref": "8", "answer_extracted": "8", "correct": true, "grade_method": "exact", "input_tokens": 92, "output_tokens": 119, "cost_usd": 0.001374, "latency_s": 1.9068386554718018, "stop_reason": "end_turn", "from_cache": false, "output_text": "The problem is ambiguous about what \"average\" means, so I take it to mean the arithmetic mean of the three grades.\n\nAdd the grades: 7 + 8 + 9 = 24.\n\nDivide by the number of grades: 24 / 3 = 8.\n\nThe average is 8. (The median is also 8, so the answer is the same under either reading.)\n\n\\boxed{8}"}
{"uid": "own/0013", "dataset": "own", "topic": "statistics", "model_alias": "opus", "model_id": "claude-opus-5-5", "answer_ref": "8", "answer_extracted": "8", "correct": true, "grade_method": "exact", "input_tokens": 92, "output_tokens": 66, "cost_usd": 0.001688, "latency_s": 1.6571216583251953, "stop_reason": "end_turn", "from_cache": false, "output_text": "Add the three grades: 7 + 8 + 9 = 24.\n\nDivide by the number of grades: 24 ÷ 3 = 8.\n\nThe average grade is 8.\n\n\\boxed{8}"}
{"uid": "own/0014", "dataset": "own", "topic": "proportionality", "model_alias": "haiku", "model_id": "claude-haiku-5-5", "answer_ref": "3", "answer_extracted": "3", "correct": true, "grade_method": "exact", "input_tokens": 107, "output_tokens": 107, "cost_usd": 6.42e-05, "latency_s": 1.7630655765533447, "stop_reason": "end_turn", "from_cache": false, "output_text": "Total work is proportional to (number of workers) × (number of days). With 4 workers over 6 days, the total work is 4 × 6 = 24 worker-days.\n\nWith 8 workers working at the same rate, the time needed is\n\nDays = 24 / 8 = 3.\n\n**Answer: 3 days**\n\n\\boxed{3}"}
